Package: tracegamma
Type: Package
Title: The Trace-Gamma Calibrated Reference for Quadratic-Form Tests
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("William J.", "Dwyer", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "wjdwyer@trialdesign.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-0855-7222"))
Description: The trace-gamma distribution is the closed-form shifted, scaled
    chi-square matched to the first three cumulants of a quadratic form in
    near-normal variables. Those cumulants are exact traces of one matrix
    product (Lancaster, 1954), and the three-moment fit is that of Solomon and
    Stephens (1977). Welch's F is the two-cumulant member of the family and
    Pearson's chi-square the equal-eigenvalue member, so the family contains
    the classical references rather than competing with them. Also provides the
    exact generalized chi-square by Imhof (1961) numerical inversion, for
    checking the closed form against the truth rather than against simulation,
    the kurtosis and tail-rate defects that govern the approximation error, and
    an estimable correction for non-normal inputs.
